<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0006 2010-03-26 — Rubavu</name><styleUrl>#IFRC, Rwanda: Rubavu Landslide DREF Final Report, 2010, https://reliefweb.int/report/rwanda/rwanda-rubavu-landslide-dref-operation-n%C2%B0-mdrrw006-final-report</styleUrl><description>date: 2010-03-26; province: Western; district: Rubavu; sector: Rubavu; place_description: Hills around Mount Rubavu; landslide_type: mudslide/landslide; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: ±50 km; broad catalog point; confidence: IFRC, Rwanda: Rubavu Landslide DREF Final Report, 2010, https://reliefweb.int/report/rwanda/rwanda-rubavu-landslide-dref-operation-n%C2%B0-mdrrw006-final-report</description><Point><coordinates>29.371100,-1.698500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0008 2013-05-05/06 — Gakenke</name><styleUrl>#Medium</styleUrl><description>date: 2013-05-05/06; province: Northern; district: Gakenke; place_description: Gashenyi, Kigali–Musanze/Gisenyi highway; landslide_type: landslide/road-slope failure; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: unknown (NASA catalog field); confidence: Medium; notes: NASA GLC says 5 May; 7 May eTurboNews says “yesterday” (6 May). Coordinate is catalog-reported and accuracy was not stated; retained as a location cue, not an exact failure point.</description><Point><coordinates>29.835300,-1.664900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0011 2016-05-07 — Gakenke</name><styleUrl>#High</styleUrl><description>date: 2016-05-07; province: Northern; district: Gakenke; place_description: Northern Rwanda heavy-rain disaster episode; landslide_type: landslides/mudslides with floods; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: ±25 km (NASA GLC); confidence: High; notes: FEWS NET reports 54 deaths for Gakenke+Ngororero and planned resettlement of ~28,000 people; contemporaneous news reports 49 nationally at an earlier update. These are not allocated to this point. NASA also lists a second Ngororero point for this same episode; one record per mapped district location is kept below.</description><Point><coordinates>29.803300,-1.710100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0012 2016-05-07 — Ngororero</name><styleUrl>#High</styleUrl><description>date: 2016-05-07; province: Western; district: Ngororero; place_description: Ngororero District, Northern/Western episode; landslide_type: landslides/mudslides with floods; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: ±25 km (NASA GLC); confidence: High; notes: Catalog point is broad and event-level impact totals are shared with Gakenke; not district-attributed. Same disaster episode as RWA-LS-0011.</description><Point><coordinates>29.594800,-1.824500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0013 2016-12-06 — Gasabo</name><styleUrl>#High</styleUrl><description>date: 2016-12-06; province: Kigali City; district: Gasabo; sector: Nduba; place_description: Crystal Mining Trading Company cassiterite concession; landslide_type: mining-cliff landslide/slope failure; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: ±5 km (NASA GLC); confidence: High; notes: Rwanda National Police independently confirms date, Nduba sector and death. Catalog point passes Rwanda bounds and is consistent with Gasabo at district-scale, not a survey location.</description><Point><coordinates>30.114407,-1.852959,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0014 2018-03-03 — Rubavu</name><styleUrl>#High</styleUrl><description>date: 2018-03-03; province: Western; district: Rubavu; sector: Nyundo; Nyakiliba; Rugerero; Kanama; place_description: Sebeya River and other Rubavu areas; landslide_type: landslides with flooding; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: district/event point; accuracy not stated; confidence: High; notes: The HDX/GLIDE point is broad; coordinates are an inventory-reported point, not a mapped slide centroid. The GLIDE fatality field is 0; this means no fatalities recorded in this row, not proof none occurred.</description><Point><coordinates>29.3714909,-1.6986475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>RWA-LS-0023 2023-05-06 — Rubavu</name><styleUrl>#High</styleUrl><description>date: 2023-05-06; province: Western; district: Rubavu; place_description: Sebaya River / Nyundo area (UNOSAT AOI 1-2); landslide_type: landslide/mudslide; coordinate_accuracy_estimate: assessment AOI center; imagery 50 cm, not slide-point accuracy; confidence: High; notes: UNOSAT AOI image-center coordinate 1°42′07″S 29°19′21″E. Coordinates locate the assessment area, not the landslide scar centroid; 50 cm imagery; preliminary and not field validated.</description><Point><coordinates>29.322500,-1.701944,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
